{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "label": "Supply chain", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Answers one question about the published package: how much of it can you check rather than trust.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_npm_provenance", "label": "npm provenance via Trusted Publishing", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The workflow exchanges a short-lived GitHub identity token for a one-shot publish token, so there is no long-lived npm token to leak; npm audit signatures verifies the attestation.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_cyclonedx_sbom", "label": "CycloneDX SBOM release asset", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Generated from the installed tree and attached to the GitHub Release, so you can answer whether a release was affected by an advisory without reconstructing the closure from a lockfile.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_dependency_graph_gap", "label": "The dependency graph is not the SBOM", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "GitHub dependency graph records the unresolved ranges from package.json and misses transitive packages entirely, so Dependabot alerts and dependency-review-action describe something other than what shipped.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_codeql", "label": "CodeQL analysis", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Runs on pull requests, on pushes to main and develop, and weekly - the weekly run is not redundant because CodeQL ships new queries, so a file clean when written can be flagged months later.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_advisory_gate", "label": "bun audit advisory gate", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Reads bun.lock so it sees the versions that actually ship, which is why it is bun audit rather than dependency-review-action; a weekly cron catches advisories published against an unchanged lockfile.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_suppression_list_parity", "label": "Advisory suppression list parity", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Pre-existing advisories are suppressed by ID and listed in SECURITY.md; a test fails if the two sets drift apart, so the set cannot grow quietly.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_pinned_actions", "label": "SHA-pinned workflow actions", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A tag is a mutable pointer, so whoever can move actions/checkout@v7 runs arbitrary code inside the job that publishes to npm; a SHA cannot be repointed and the trailing tag comment keeps Dependabot updating the pins.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_frozen_installs_least_privilege", "label": "Frozen installs and least privilege", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Every CI install is frozen-lockfile so a green check never means passed against an irreproducible dependency set; job tokens are read-only by default and no job that can write to the repository runs third-party install scripts.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_workflow_hygiene_test", "label": "WorkflowHygiene test", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Workflow YAML is invisible to the type checker, so without an assertion on every bun test a hardening decision decays the first time somebody edits a file without knowing about it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_scope_boundary", "label": "Vulnerability scope boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The plain-TCP cluster default ships on purpose and is documented alongside the hardening recipe, so it is not a vulnerability; a documented mitigation that does not deliver what it promises is one.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_npm_provenance"